meta {
  name: 16 Create Report Attachment
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/attachments
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "document",
    "fileUrl": "https://s3-ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com/stage.ez.reports/uploads/finance-attachments/demo/report.pdf",
    "fileName": "report.pdf",
    "notes": "Reference document",
    "fileSizeBytes": 12345
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.body && res.body.success && res.body.data;
  if (data && data.id) bru.setVar("labReportAttachmentId", data.id);
}

docs {
  Persist an already-uploaded file against a report. Upload the bytes **first** via
  `POST /uploads/attachment` (S3) to get `fileUrl`, then send it here.

  **Body**
  - `kind` (required) — `image` | `document` | `file` (the entry-modal buckets).
  - `fileUrl` (required, url) — the S3 URL from `POST /uploads/attachment`.
  - `fileName` (required) — display name.
  - `notes` (optional) — caption.
  - `fileSizeBytes` (optional, int) — the `size` returned by `POST /uploads/attachment`;
    summed to enforce the per-report File+ total-size limit.

  **PDF or raster image for `kind: "file"`** — a `file` upload (the Test Entry
  "File +" button) must be a PDF or a raster image (`fileName`/`fileUrl` ending in
  `.pdf`/`.png`/`.jpg`/`.jpeg`/`.webp`/`.gif` — **SVG is not accepted**); these
  feed the `{test_file_attachment}` print tag — a PDF is embedded as pages, an
  image is rendered via `<img>`. `image` / `document` uploads accept their usual types.

  **File+ limits (per report):** at most **10** File attachments and **25 MB** total
  (409/422 `TOO_MANY_TEST_FILE_ATTACHMENTS` / `TEST_FILE_ATTACHMENTS_TOO_LARGE`).

  Negative case — rejected with a 400 validation error ("Only PDF or image files
  can be attached with the File button"):
  ```json
  { "kind": "file", "fileUrl": "https://.../qc-results.xlsx", "fileName": "qc-results.xlsx" }
  ```

  Note: `POST /uploads/attachment` also verifies the file's **content** (magic bytes)
  matches its declared type and returns `{ url, size }` (the `size` goes in `fileSizeBytes`).

  Gated on the technician-notes permission. The same table backs the EMI histogram
  images, so both show in `GET .../attachments`. Captures `labReportAttachmentId`.
}
